meta {
  name: start
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/auth/rotate/start
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{sessionToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "registrationRequest": "<base64 output of a real OpaqueClient.registerInit() for the NEW password -- see ../README.md>"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.continuityChallenge) {
    bru.setEnvVar("continuityChallenge", res.body.continuityChallenge);
  }
}

docs {
  RotationAuthGuard accepts sessionToken OR refreshToken -- both work
  here. registrationRequest needs real OPAQUE client math, same
  limitation as auth/register-start (see ../README.md) -- this request
  only documents the shape.

  Before 2026-09-15, sending the placeholder body below as-is crashed
  with an uncaught 500 ("error deserializing element", several frames
  deep inside @cloudflare/voprf-ts's Group.deserialize -- an invalid
  elliptic-curve point). CloudflareOpaqueServerProvider now catches that
  and every other malformed-registrationRequest failure and returns a
  clean 400 instead: {"message": "registrationRequest is not
  well-formed OPAQUE protocol data.", "statusCode": 400}. Still not a
  usable response -- this request remains reference-only -- just no
  longer an unhandled server crash.

  opaque-bruno-fixture.mjs (2026-09-14 update) now performs a full
  rotate/start + rotate/finish round-trip itself, right after
  login/finish -- run the script for a live, real end-to-end rotation
  test. This request stays reference-only for inspecting the shape or
  manually driving a rotation with your own OpaqueClient script.

  continuityChallenge only comes back if this account was registered
  with a continuitySecret (hardened mode, see auth/register-finish's
  docs) -- otherwise it's absent and rotation/finish needs no signature.
}
